        "text": "PyCharm\nPyCharm is one of the best Python IDE editors available for Python programming and\nit is available for Windows, macOS, and Linux. It is a complete IDE tailored for Python\nprogramming, which helps programmers with code completion, debugging, refactoring,\nsmart search, access to popular database servers, integration with version control systems,\nand many more features. The IDE provides a plugin platform for developers to extend the\nbase functionalities as needed. PyCharm is available in the following formats:\n\u2022I Community version, which is free and comes for pure Python development\n\u2022I Professional version, which is not free and comes with support for web development\nsuch as HyperText Markup Language ( HTML ), JavaScript,\nand SQL",
